<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.chamber.daily-snapshot</string>

  <!--
    Runs after com.chamber.verify (08:30) so it can read that run's result
    rather than racing it.

    10:07, not 08:52. A real MiniLM ingest of ~28,500 passages takes about 75
    minutes because the embedder spawns one python subprocess per passage, so
    the 08:30 job does not reach `verify` until roughly 09:55. The original
    08:52 slot was chosen while the corpus was silently being hash-embedded,
    which took two minutes -- so this schedule was calibrated against a bug,
    and would have read a half-built index and reported it as fact.

    This job records; it does not judge. Its exit status is deliberately 0 even
    when a check inside it fails, because `chamber verify` is the gate and it
    already runs on its own schedule with its own non-zero contract. A recorder
    that also failed would produce two alerts for one event and train the
    operator to ignore both.

    Output is a dated markdown file per day, which is what makes the record
    survive a session ending -- the analysis half can be written later, by
    anyone, from a file that is still there.

    It runs the copy of the script inside the release checkout that
    `chamber pin <tag>` keeps, not the development checkout, so the report
    describes the release the 08:30 job ran and not whatever branch happens to
    be checked out at 10:07. The job's login shell expands $HOME. A release tag
    older than the one that first contains this path has the previous script,
    which calls the `chamber` on PATH; see deploy/SCHEDULING.md.
  -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/sh</string>
    <string>-lc</string>
    <string>$HOME/.local/share/chamber-release/scripts/daily-snapshot.sh</string>
  </array>

  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>10</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>7</integer>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>REPLACE_WITH_HOME/Library/Logs/chamber-daily-snapshot.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>REPLACE_WITH_HOME/Library/Logs/chamber-daily-snapshot.log</string>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
